  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g504288-d1773988-r1051115632-Discovery_Parks_Cradle_Mountain-Cradle_Mountain_Lake_St_Clair_National_Park_Tas.html",
  "title": "Punishment not pleasure",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "I will start by clarifying that we are travellers who are happy to ‘rough it’ a bit and consider location more important than accommodation. That said, this place is grubby to the point of being completely unenjoyable.\nCabins are old, musty and have no outdoor seating space or views ( no areas of the site have Mountain View’s bizarrely given the proximity to cradle mountain) \nTo escape the grimness of the cabin there is a communal outdoor bbq area but this is equally unappealing and unattractive. \nWhilst I accept that proximity to cradle mountain will warrant somewhat inflated  prices, to charge £150 a night for this is scandalous. \nWe have paid similar prices for other stays in Tasmania and they have been absolutely stunning. \nThis is poor quality hostel vibes at boutique hotel prices. \nStay further afield and visit cradle mountain on a day trip would be my advice. There is nothing enjoyable about this place unfortunately.",
  "username": "Julieanne D",
  "connectionToSubject": null,
