  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g504288-d1773988-r1042532901-Discovery_Parks_Cradle_Mountain-Cradle_Mountain_Lake_St_Clair_National_Park_Tas.html",
  "title": "King Billy Court Cabins",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "The cabin was very comfortable for 2 adults and a child.  Lovely heating from both gas and air conditioner.   Cabin was reasonably clean, but unfortunately cupboard doors above gas cooktop had gease splatter from either inefficient ducting power or users not turning on exhaust.  Plastic kettle rather than stainless steel unfortunately.  Plus was the two stainless steel saucepans but Teflon frypan.   For the price, small things lacking like glad wrap and aluminium foil, that we get in not as expensive units or cabins.\n\nBut that said, a very nice restaurant adjacent, walkable to visitor centre and smaller walks in the area.\n\nLounge dining area very nice and clean and no horrid stains from inconsiderate users.\n\nWe arrived on a very cold summer's afternoon with snow flurries and strong winds, so the warmed cabin was lovely to enter but single beds have no electric blankets unless they're put on in the winter months.\n\nBut all that said, I'd stay at these cabins again",
  "username": "janicesW6926JF",
  "connectionToSubject": null,
  "absoluteUrl": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g504288-d1773988-r1042532901-Discovery_Parks_Cradle_Mountain-Cradle_Mountain_Lake_St_Clair_National_Park_Tas.html",
