  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g504288-d1773988-r1034516764-Discovery_Parks_Cradle_Mountain-Cradle_Mountain_Lake_St_Clair_National_Park_Tas.html",
  "title": "Lovely stay at King Billy Court 4 cabin",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "I booked a deluxe 2-bedroom cabin with Discovery Resorts at Cradle Mountain for my family of four. Check-in was swift and easy.  However, we were asked to enter through staff entrance as there was a wombat waiting at the main entrance door to grab its food and vegetables sold at the reception area. It was really nice experience to bump into a wombat.\n\nI was given King Billy Court 4 cabin, the unit with the most privacy as it is the last cabin at the end of the road among the four newly built cabins, the one which is closest to nature. The cabin was new, spacious in modern design. The sofa in the living room was very comfortable. The bathroom has heated floor, and bedrooms come with heated blanket. \n\nThe kitchenette also looks new. However, the kitchen utensils were not complete, kitchenware like plates and bowls were limited and oven mitten was not provided, hence it was a little challenging to remove cooked food from the oven. This is the only downside of the stay. \n\nOverall, my family and I enjoyed our stay very much and will definitely return if we visit Cradle Mountain again.",
  "username": "Mike_Wong75",
  "connectionToSubject": null,
